<title>USA: Alabama jobless rate edges up to 4.5 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Alabama jobless rate edges up to 4.5 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>MONTGOMERY, Ala. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alabama's unemployment rate edged up to 4.5 percent in March from 4.4 percent in February, the state Department of Industrial Relations said Thursday.</p>
<p>The small increase was attributed to manufacturing job losses, mainly in textiles and apparel, and was not considered significant.</p>
<p>The state jobless rate has remained below five percent for eight consecutive months.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
